From: Zenith
Subject: es-audio-48k: open the SDL_mixer device at 48 kHz

The RK3326 audio sink runs at 48000 Hz. ES opened its mixer at 44100 Hz, so pipewire resampled the stream on every
cycle (the open stream feeds silence even when nothing plays): ~9.6% of a core between pipewire and pipewire-pulse
while the menu was idle. Measured: forcing the sink to 44100 Hz halves that cost. Opening at 48000 Hz avoids the resampling.
---
--- a/es-core/src/AudioManager.cpp	2026-10-08 23:34:42.349963815 +0200
+++ b/es-core/src/AudioManager.cpp	2026-10-08 23:34:42.837039840 +0200
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@
 	}
 
 	// Open the audio device and pause
-	if (Mix_OpenAudio(44100, MIX_DEFAULT_FORMAT, 2, 4096) < 0)
+	if (Mix_OpenAudio(48000, MIX_DEFAULT_FORMAT, 2, 4096) < 0)
 	{
 		mMusicVolume = 0;
 		LOG(LogError) << "MUSIC Error - Unable to open SDLMixer audio: " << SDL_GetError() << std::endl;
